Music Map

	Philosophy

		-
			A music map is a codified protocol for a text which specifies the durations of, and
			intervals between, the syllables, and the pitches with which to recite said syllables.

			A music map which only specifies the durations and intervals is called a rhythm map,
			and a music map which only specifies the pitches is called a melody map.
		-

	Principles

		Music Mapper

			-
				A music mapper is an algorithm or process which generates music maps for arbitrary
				text.

				Music mappers may take specified configurations into account when rendering music
				maps.
			-